That concludes the Secure Boot setup. In future, systemd will be used to sign
files for Scure Boot. If you would like, you can now remove the sbsigntools
package.

You should now reboot the system and run "%1 10" or "%1 secureboot" to execute
the current step again. When asked, do not choose to skip it! If everything went
as expected, the script will let you know that Secure Boot is already active.
You will then be taken to the next step.